# The reviewed exceptions of the Trivy scans of the Computer Image, the
# Headless Server image and each Server Package (xtask/src/advisories.rs).
#
# Put each exception on a line of its own: the advisory ID alone. Put its
# reason in a comment on the line above it: how an installation can reach
# the finding, and which update was checked. Record a finding here only
# after the update path is checked. A finding that an update removes is not
# an exception: update the component.

# brace-expansion 5.0.9 in the npm of the Computer Image. It expands the
# glob patterns of npm commands that the Agent runs on its own Computer,
# so a crafted pattern stops only that npm command. npm 11.20.0, the
# latest 11 release, and npm 12.1.0, the latest release, both bundle
# brace-expansion 5.0.9. The maintainer accepted this exception.
CVE-2026-102276
# The second brace-expansion advisory, with the same reason and check.
CVE-2026-102278

# undici 6.28.0 in the npm of the Computer Image. npm uses it for its own
# registry requests on the Agent's Computer, and a malicious WebSocket
# server can stop only that npm process. npm 11.20.0 and npm 12.1.0 both
# bundle undici 6.28.0. pnpm 11.28.2 bundles the fixed undici 6.28.1.
# The maintainer accepted this exception.
CVE-2026-19534

# The Go standard library 1.27.1 in gog, which the Headless Server image
# and each Server Package bundle. The flaw makes an HTTP server that
# serves Range requests through FileServer, ServeFile or ServeContent use
# excessive CPU. Pagis runs gog as a command-line client for each Google
# tool call and never runs its only server command, `gmail watch serve`,
# which serves no file. Go 1.27.2 has the fix. gog 0.42.0 and gog 0.43.0,
# the latest release, are both built with Go 1.27.1. The maintainer
# accepted this exception.
CVE-2026-78667
# The second Go standard library advisory in gog: a TLS server that
# accepts Encrypted Client Hello can exhaust its memory. gog makes TLS
# connections only as a client. The update check is the same.
CVE-2026-97031
